SUMMARY:Experimental Testing of Anticonformity to Depolarize Social System
DTSTART:20261020T130000Z
DTEND:20261020T133000Z
DTSTAMP:20261016T090631Z
UID:0c75ea1398ff9f9ccd5553f1@systemsmap.antlerboy.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Complexity
DESCRIPTION:Complexity Science Hub\nAnticonformity\, or going against the 
 group norm\, as a form of social response has been studied in computationa
 l models. But empirically\, we still don't know if anticonformity can be e
 ncouraged to a level sufficient to reduce polarization of opinions. They i
 nvestigate this using an interactive group experiments where we gave some 
 people an encouragement to stand out to help their group reconsiders \nLan
 guage: Not specified\nLanguage requirements: Not specified\nInterpretation
 : Not specified\nAccess: See organiser\nhttps://csh.ac.at/events/experimen
 tal-testing-of-anticonformity-to-depolarize-social-system/\nNo longer foun
 d in the latest source listing\; confirmation needed.\nThis event could no
